      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSituated in the peaceful rural setting of Girley, Fordstown, this impressive four-bedroom detached family home offers spacious living, stylish interiors, and a wonderful outdoor setting, making it ideal for modern family life.\n\nPresented in good condition throughout, the property boasts a contemporary and tasteful finish, with bright and well-proportioned accommodation designed to maximise comfort and natural light. The interior spaces flow well for both everyday living and entertaining, while the overall layout provides ample room for growing families.\n\nTo the rear, the property enjoys a very large back garden, offering excellent privacy and plenty of space for outdoor dining, recreation, or future landscaping. To the front, the home overlooks a beautiful communal green area, with the property benefiting from a quarter ownership share, creating a safe and open environment and adding to the sense of space surrounding the home.\n\nThe location offers the perfect balance of countryside tranquillity and convenience. The nearby villages of Kells and Athboy provide a wide range of everyday amenities including shops, cafés, schools, and sporting facilities. Families are well catered for with several respected primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area.\n\nFor commuters, the property benefits from excellent road connectivity with easy access to the M3 Motorway, allowing straightforward travel to Navan, Dublin, and beyond.\n\nA particular highlight of the location is its close proximity to Causey Farm, a great family location with unique seasonal events and JoeThePro Driving Range, a popular golf practice facility located just minutes away, offering an excellent leisure amenity right on your doorstep.\n\nCombining style, generous outdoor space, and a highly convenient rural location, this superb property represents a fantastic opportunity to acquire a quality home in a peaceful yet well-connected setting in County Meath.\nEarly viewing is advised."
      },
